Scenario 1: Customer Deliveries
Tables: users (user_id, user_name) and shipments (shipment_id, user_id, status)
Task: Show the user_name and shipment_id for shipments where status = 'Delivered'.

1, select u.username, s.shipment_id
from users as u inner join shipments as s
on u.user_id = s.user_id
where status = 'delivered';

Scenario 2: Doctor Appointments
Tables: doctors (doctor_id, doctor_name, specialty) and consultations (consultation_id, doctor_id, patient_name)
Task: List the doctor_name and patient_name for consultations where the doctor's specialty = 'Cardiology'.

2, select d.doctor_name, c.patient_name
from doctors as d inner join consultations as c
on d.doctor_id = c.doctor_id
where speciality = 'cardiology';

Scenario 3: Product Inventory
Tables: products (product_id, product_name, category) and inventory (item_id, product_id, stock_count)
Task: Return product_name and stock_count for products in the 'Electronics' category.

3, select p.product_name, i.stock_count
from products as p inner join inventory as i
on p.product_id = i.product_id
where category = 'electronics';

Scenario 4: Flight Bookings
Tables: passengers (passenger_id, passenger_name) and tickets (ticket_id, passenger_id, class_type, price)
Task: Show passenger_name and price for tickets where class_type = 'First Class' and price > 1000.

4, select p.passengers_name, t.price
from passengers as p inner join tickets as t
on p.passenger_id = t.passenger_id
where class_type = 'first class' and price > 1000;

Scenario: Customer Loyalty Tiers
Table A: users (user_id, username)
Table B: payments (payment_id, user_id, amount, status)
Task: Write a query that joins both tables to calculate each user's username and their total paid amount (SUM(amount) AS total_paid).
Only include payments where status = 'Success'.
Group by username.
Add a CASE WHEN column called tier:
'VIP' when SUM(amount) >= 500
'Regular' for all others (ELSE)
Order by total_paid DESC.

SELECT 
    c.name, 
    SUM(o.amount) AS total_spent
FROM customers AS c 
INNER JOIN orders AS o
    ON c.customer_id = o.customer_id
WHERE o.status = 'Completed'
GROUP BY c.customer_id, c.name
HAVING SUM(o.amount) > 200
ORDER BY total_spent DESC;

